:pack   Treasure Trash — Act 1 (raccoon only, crow pinned)
:format 1
;
; legend  # wall  - floor  @ raccoon  $ bag  C full can  c empty can
;         x spilled trash  E exit  + raccoon on exit
; There is no glyph for anything else on an exit: the rules refuse any action that would
; put an object there, so no reachable state needs one.
;
; Every field below is machine-checked by verify.mjs — :par must be the provably
; minimal solve, :solve must replay to a win in exactly :par actions, and :traps must
; equal the number of legal actions that lead to an unwinnable board.
;
; Note how low :traps is: the exit refuses anything that would land on it, so the whole
; class of "you buried your own way out" soft-locks is now a refusal at the keypress.
;
; :arm on = board-changing actions ask twice in this room. It is a scaffold for the room
; that INTRODUCES a piece (L1 the bag, L2 the can) and comes off once the verb is known.
; Default is off. It is input-only: it cannot change a par, and the solver never sees it.

:level  L0
:name   Out
:teach  the exit
:par    2
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  uu
:note   No bags, so the exit is live from move one. Walk forward and leave.
:grid
#E#
#-#
#@#
:end

:level  L1
:name   Pounce
:teach  directional pounce, the fan, permanent mess
:arm    on
:par    4
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  uU!dr
:note   The down-strike is refused: its fan would land on the exit at (3,3).
:grid
---
-$-
--E
#@#
:end

:level  L2
:name   Heavy Can
:teach  the can, and that where you park your junk is half the job
:arm    on
:par    7
:traps  1
:solves 1
:solve  UluRU!dl
:note   Shoving the can left is refused — the exit will not take it. Right is the way.
:grid
---
---
E--
-C-
-@-
:end

:level  L3
:name   Fire Away From the Path
:teach  fire your mess away from where you still need to walk
:par    5
:traps  2
:solves 2
:solve  U!dD!ur
:note   Either bag struck toward the corridor is refused — the exit is in that fan.
:grid
---
-$-
-@E
-$-
---
:end

:level  L4
:name   Right Beside the Door
:teach  a bag sitting next to the exit has exactly one legal direction — away from it
:par    5
:traps  3
:solves 1
:solve  D!uuR!l
:note   Three of the top bag's four directions put trash on the exit and are refused, so you fire it from the exit itself.
:grid
----
-E$-
-@--
-$--
----
:end

:level  L5
:name   Recycling Day
:teach  the recycle bin — shifting it costs you a cell of floor, and only one way is legal
:arm    on
:par    6
:traps  1
:solves 1
:solve  luRU!dl
:note   The bin stands on the cell you must strike from. Shoving it left is refused (the exit will not take it), so it goes right — and drops a cell of trash two along as it goes.
:grid
-----
--$--
-Eb--
--@--
-----
:end

:level  L6
:name   Runaway Bin
:teach  the wheelie bin rolls until something stops it, and drops its bag out the back
:arm    on
:par    11
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  UluuRdR!lddd
:note   You choose the wall it hits, not where it stops. The bag lands behind it, so the emptied bin — which still rolls — is what stands between you and the bag you just freed.
:grid
-----
--W--
--@--
-----
-E---
:end




:level  L7
:name   Three Bags Full
:teach  three bags and no containers — the first room that is only about order
:par    13
:traps  13
:solves 1
:solve  lldR!ldD!ulluR!l
:note   Every strike closes cells the other two still need. No piece to relocate and nowhere to put the mess but the floor.
:grid
----@
E$-$-
-----
--$--
-----
:end

:level  L8
:name   Bin Night
:teach  both containers at once — the can that ejects a bag and the bin that drops trash
:par    15
:traps  7
:solves 1
:solve  lDldL!rurrdLLdR!l
:note   The can hands you a second bag to deal with and the bin charges you a cell of floor. Neither can be left where it stands.
:grid
-b--@
---C-
-$---
--E--
-----
-----
:end

:level  L9
:name   Tight Corner
:teach  the exit wedged between two bags and the bin that can bury the way through
:par    17
:traps  3
:solves 2
:solve  uruullDurrddD!ulU!d
:note   Only three ways to lose this one, and all of them are the same mistake: filling the gap you have to come back through.
:grid
------
------
b$----
-E----
-@$---
------
:end

:level  L10
:name   Long Way Round
:teach  the wheelie bin again, now with the walk home as part of the cost
:par    19
:traps  16
:solves 1
:solve  uuulDdddlU!drrddLuL!r
:note   The bin rolls away from the exit, so freeing the bag and reaching the door pull in opposite directions.
:grid
-----
---W-
--$--
----@
----E
-----
:end

:level  L11
:name   Crosstown
:teach  two bags on opposite corners with one rolling bin between them
:par    21
:traps  34
:solves 1
:solve  rrUuurD!ulluuRdR!lulD!ul
:note   The bin is the only piece that crosses the board, and it only crosses once per shove.
:grid
E-----
-$----
------
---W$-
-@----
------
:end

:level  L12
:name   The Far Side
:teach  a bag and a bin parked as far from the exit as the room allows
:par    23
:traps  12
:solves 3
:solve  uuuurrDdL!rddrddLuL!ruuuu
:note   Nothing here is subtle. The room is long because the pieces are far apart and the bin will not stop where you want it.
:grid
----E-
--$W--
------
------
-@----
------
:end

:level  L13
:name   Closing Time
:teach  everything the pack has taught, at the longest range it has asked for
:par    25
:traps  43
:solves 2
:solve  uuuulDddlU!ddddRrU!dlllluR!l
:note   Two bags, a rolling bin, and an exit on the far wall. The last room in the pack and the only one that needs all of it at once.
:grid
------
---$W-
------
------
E$---@
------
:end

:level  L14
:name   Wet Paws
:teach  water — he won't cross it, but he'll walk on what he throws in it
:arm    on
:par    7
:traps  0
:solves 1
:solve  R!uuluR!l
:note   The canal is the only thing between him and the exit, and the first move you try walks straight into it. A fan fired sideways drops two of its five cells in the water; those two are now floor. Nothing here can be lost — the room has no traps at all.
:grid
----
-E$-
----
~~~~
-@$-
----
:end

:level  L15
:name   Two Crossings
:teach  order — one bag builds the way to another, so the wrong first tear strands you
:par    10
:traps  8
:solves 1
:solve  R!uulL!dD!uur
:note   Three bags, two of them spent on the canal. Opening the left bag first loses the room in every direction — its fan seals the only route to the bag that builds your crossing. The first room in the pack where WHICH bag, not which way, is the question.
:grid
-----
-$E--
~~~~~
-$@$-
-----
:end

:level  L16
:name   Wet the Landing
:teach  the water jug — wet the cell your own fan is about to hit, and the trash lands as floor
:arm    on
:par    6
:traps  5
:solves 1
:solve  UruU!ll
:note   The fan is going to hit (3,2) whichever way you play it. Leave it dry and that cell becomes trash, a wall between you and the door; shove the jug up first and it becomes water, and the same fan fills it in as a bridge. Two moves cheaper than walking round, and the whole piece in one strike.
:grid
-----
-E-$-
-----
--j--
--@--
:end
